## Prerequisites
- Android device or emulator with ADB access
- Target app (`{{ package_name }}`) installed
- `adb` command-line tool
- Optional: Drozer framework for advanced testing

## Steps to Reproduce

### 1. Verify Component is Exported
```bash
# Check if the component is exported
adb shell dumpsys package {{ package_name }} | grep -A 10 "{{ class_name.split('.')[-1] if class_name else 'TargetActivity' }}"

# List all exported components
adb shell dumpsys package {{ package_name }} | grep -B 2 "exported=true"
```

{% if "Activity" in class_name or "activity" in class_name.lower() %}
### 2. Launch Exported Activity
```bash
# Direct launch
adb shell am start -n {{ package_name }}/{{ class_name }}

# Launch with intent extras
adb shell am start -n {{ package_name }}/{{ class_name }} \
  --es "url" "https://attacker.com" \
  --es "token" "test123" \
  --ez "admin" true

# Launch with data URI
adb shell am start -n {{ package_name }}/{{ class_name }} \
  -d "file:///data/data/{{ package_name }}/databases/app.db"
```

### 3. Test for Intent Injection
```bash
# Send crafted intents with sensitive parameters
adb shell am start -n {{ package_name }}/{{ class_name }} \
  --es "redirect_url" "https://evil.com" \
  --ei "user_id" 1 \
  --es "action" "delete_account"
```
{% endif %}

{% if "Service" in class_name or "service" in class_name.lower() %}
